WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:47.841
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:48.111 --> 00:55.076
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

3
00:56.327 --> 00:59.247
The pneumatic tube system opening ceremony is a major event

4
00:59.330 --> 01:02.333
attended by high-ranking officials like Gyeongseong's mayor,

5
01:02.417 --> 01:04.919
the Central Advisory Council's vice chair, foreign reporters,

6
01:05.003 --> 01:07.046
and pro-Japanese businessmen like Kim Seung-eok.

7
01:07.130 --> 01:09.215
Among us, Philip and I will be attending.

8
01:09.966 --> 01:11.843
Myung-nam, who is invited with her father,

9
01:11.926 --> 01:14.846
and Songjeon will also be there.

10
01:14.929 --> 01:18.183
Songjeon, is it confirmed that you'll be working as a kitchen assistant?

11
01:18.766 --> 01:23.438
Yes, since I'm Japanese, I passed the background check without issue.

12
01:23.521 --> 01:25.440
Thank you for taking on this dangerous job.

13
01:25.523 --> 01:27.275
I'm a member of the Gugukdan too.

14
01:27.859 --> 01:29.360
On the day of the opening ceremony…

15
01:29.444 --> 01:31.446
LADIES' ROOM

16
01:38.119 --> 01:41.831
I'll retrieve the three bombs we've smuggled in

17
01:41.915 --> 01:43.625
and assemble them into time bombs.

18
01:54.719 --> 01:56.054
At 6:00 p.m.,

19
01:56.137 --> 01:59.224
the ceremony will begin in the pneumatic tube room on the first floor.

20
01:59.307 --> 02:03.853
The governor-general, the inspector general, Philip, and others will attend.

21
02:09.400 --> 02:12.654
Meanwhile, Myung-nam and I will wait with the other guests

22
02:12.737 --> 02:14.405
in the second-floor banquet hall.

23
02:14.489 --> 02:15.949
Oh my, Ms. Myung-nam.

24
02:16.741 --> 02:17.951
Hello.

25
02:32.382 --> 02:33.216
When the time comes…

26
02:33.299 --> 02:34.926
Fire!

27
02:35.009 --> 02:37.345
Songjeon will set off the fire alarm

28
02:37.428 --> 02:40.139
to distract the guests in the banquet hall.

29
02:45.228 --> 02:46.062
Yes, sir!

30
02:46.813 --> 02:48.731
-Go see what's happening. -Yes, sir!

31
02:52.151 --> 02:53.194
Are you hurt?

32
02:53.278 --> 02:54.988
What is going on?

33
02:55.071 --> 02:56.239
I'm sorry.

34
02:56.322 --> 03:00.118
I'll hide the bomb in the floral arrangement on the stage.

35
03:13.881 --> 03:16.801
It'll be right in front of where the governor-general

36
03:17.510 --> 03:20.930
and inspector general will stand when they return after the ceremony.

37
03:21.639 --> 03:23.725
His Excellency the Governor-General is arriving!

38
04:02.096 --> 04:03.264
Raise your glasses!

39
04:12.106 --> 04:13.358
As for the bomb,

40
04:13.441 --> 04:15.902
when the governor-general proposes a toast…

41
04:18.571 --> 04:19.822
Cheers!

42
04:19.906 --> 04:21.324
-Cheers! -Cheers!

43
04:21.407 --> 04:23.201
-Cheers! -Cheers!

44
04:29.749 --> 04:30.792
…it will go off.

45
05:00.029 --> 05:06.494
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

46
05:07.537 --> 05:09.831
EPISODE 9

47
05:14.419 --> 05:15.336
You're late.

48
05:32.520 --> 05:35.022
What's this?

49
05:36.107 --> 05:37.692
It's an identity guarantee letter.

50
05:40.027 --> 05:41.612
An identity guarantee letter?

51
05:42.738 --> 05:44.824
You'll be leaving tomorrow night

52
05:45.658 --> 05:46.576
for America.

53
05:47.243 --> 05:48.453
Tomorrow?

54
05:48.536 --> 05:49.412
That's right.

55
05:50.204 --> 05:53.666
The American missionary, Mr. Miller, is returning to America with his family.

56
05:55.126 --> 05:59.755
Mrs. Miller is taking a nanny to America to care for her three-month-old baby.

57
06:00.506 --> 06:01.549
The nanny's name is

58
06:02.550 --> 06:03.509
Keum Seo-hee.

59
06:05.303 --> 06:08.639
It's a document where Mr. Miller guarantees your identity.

60
06:08.723 --> 06:11.767
Philip went to a lot of trouble to get it notarized at the U.S. Consulate.

61
06:11.851 --> 06:14.020
Mr. Miller helped a great deal too.

62
06:18.941 --> 06:22.111
There's one catch. According to the document,

63
06:22.195 --> 06:26.491
you'll have to leave America within 30 days of entering the country.

64
06:27.909 --> 06:31.579
Once you arrive in San Francisco with the Miller family,

65
06:31.662 --> 06:34.499
you'll be on your own.

66
06:35.333 --> 06:37.084
You'll be staying illegally,

67
06:37.877 --> 06:39.962
but it's the best we can do. I hope you understand.

68
06:42.798 --> 06:43.633
Sure.

69
06:44.383 --> 06:45.885
Don't worry about me.

70
07:08.491 --> 07:10.451
Don't worry about the banquet tomorrow.

71
07:11.077 --> 07:13.454
We've been cracking down on independence fighters' hideouts

72
07:13.538 --> 07:15.331
in Keijo since last week.

73
07:16.123 --> 07:18.834
So far, we've arrested six independence fighters

74
07:18.918 --> 07:20.628
and 57 suspicious individuals.

75
07:22.421 --> 07:23.673
Apologies for the interruption.

76
07:37.144 --> 07:39.063
Allow me to pour you a drink.

77
07:39.146 --> 07:40.231
Get out.

78
07:57.957 --> 07:59.917
They must've mistaken this for another room.

79
08:00.001 --> 08:02.378
I'll have a serious word with the owner.

80
08:03.045 --> 08:06.090
They should know you don't like having geisha around.

81
08:11.429 --> 08:12.555
My apologies.

82
08:13.431 --> 08:15.016
I spoke out of turn.

83
08:15.099 --> 08:17.643
Any news on Keum Seok-jung's wife yet?

84
08:19.228 --> 08:21.981
We're still following leads in the Kyeam-ri area.

85
08:22.064 --> 08:24.692
We'll find out for certain as soon as possible.

86
08:24.775 --> 08:27.570
Find out how she's living if she's alive,

87
08:27.653 --> 08:29.905
or how she died if she's dead.

88
08:31.240 --> 08:33.826
Joseon women can be reckless.

89
08:35.369 --> 08:37.330
We need to tie up all the loose ends.

90
08:38.748 --> 08:40.625
Understood, sir!

91
08:44.712 --> 08:45.921
Let me pour you another drink.

92
09:03.356 --> 09:06.400
You chose to become Japanese. No one forced you.

93
09:06.484 --> 09:09.612
Remember who's given you this life of luxury all this time.

94
09:10.613 --> 09:11.989
However foolish you may be,

95
09:12.073 --> 09:14.200
you should know you owe me some gratitude.

96
09:16.661 --> 09:18.329
I really didn't steal anything.

97
09:18.412 --> 09:19.872
We were just looking.

98
09:20.456 --> 09:21.916
What the hell are you yapping about?

99
09:24.335 --> 09:26.295
Please let us go. We didn't do anything.

100
09:26.379 --> 09:29.298
Hey! You got filthy water all over my clothes.

101
09:29.382 --> 09:31.050
You filthy little street rats!

102
09:31.133 --> 09:32.385
You stink!

103
09:32.468 --> 09:34.387
Please, don't beat us.

104
09:34.470 --> 09:36.389
You know what your problem is?

105
09:36.972 --> 09:39.975
You live off Japan's generosity,

106
09:40.518 --> 09:43.479
yet you never learn how to be grateful!

107
09:48.150 --> 09:49.151
Hey.

108
09:49.235 --> 09:51.070
You there, gentleman.

109
09:51.153 --> 09:52.530
Just go on your way.

110
09:55.616 --> 09:56.659
Okay?

111
09:56.742 --> 10:00.413
I said, just be on your way.

112
10:04.166 --> 10:05.334
What the hell?

113
10:05.418 --> 10:07.086
Don't you get what I'm saying?

114
10:09.171 --> 10:10.548
Are you Josenjing?

115
10:11.924 --> 10:12.758
Right?

116
10:12.842 --> 10:15.094
However well they clean up,

117
10:15.803 --> 10:18.973
Josenjings still stink like animals--

118
10:28.649 --> 10:29.525
Stop right there!

119
10:39.201 --> 10:40.077
Say that again.

120
10:41.120 --> 10:43.289
What did you say about Josenjing?

121
10:45.791 --> 10:46.625
Say that again.

122
10:47.877 --> 10:48.878
Stop!

123
11:02.725 --> 11:03.559
Get out.

124
11:05.811 --> 11:07.772
I said, get out of here, now!

125
11:10.232 --> 11:11.650
Did you find that amusing?

126
11:12.276 --> 11:14.320
I said I didn't know

127
11:15.488 --> 11:17.531
whether to side with Joseon or Japan.

128
11:18.991 --> 11:20.409
You think I deserve this?

129
11:22.495 --> 11:23.370
Get out.

130
11:25.581 --> 11:27.541
Get out of my sight right now!

131
11:34.340 --> 11:35.966
He wanted me gone so badly.

132
11:38.886 --> 11:40.638
Now I'm actually leaving.

133
11:43.849 --> 11:45.267
Stop or I'll shoot you.

134
11:46.143 --> 11:47.561
Put your hands up and turn around.

135
11:55.611 --> 11:56.445
Go ahead.

136
11:57.905 --> 11:58.739
What?

137
11:59.406 --> 12:00.282
You said you'd shoot.

138
12:00.366 --> 12:01.784
What the hell are you saying?

139
12:01.867 --> 12:04.662
I said, shoot me. That's what you people do best.

140
12:04.745 --> 12:06.914
Kill him, Officer Kimura!

141
12:09.250 --> 12:10.459
What's your name?

142
12:11.794 --> 12:14.171
I said, what's your name?

143
12:18.592 --> 12:20.636
I want you to contact me directly.

144
12:20.719 --> 12:22.638
The Government-General, not the residence.

145
12:25.432 --> 12:26.809
Please forgive us!

146
12:28.269 --> 12:29.395
Apologize to him now!

147
12:29.478 --> 12:32.314
This gentleman is Mr. Sato Hideo, son of the inspector general

148
12:32.398 --> 12:34.024
of the Government-General.

149
12:34.108 --> 12:35.734
-Forgive us! -Forgive us!

150
12:37.069 --> 12:38.445
We made a grave mistake.

151
12:38.529 --> 12:40.489
Please forgive us!

152
12:40.573 --> 12:41.949
Please forgive us!

153
12:45.119 --> 12:47.246
We have the utmost respect

154
12:47.329 --> 12:49.248
for Inspector General Sato Shinichi!

155
13:35.628 --> 13:37.004
Welcome back.

156
13:37.087 --> 13:38.339
Welcome back.

157
13:53.312 --> 13:54.188
By the way…

158
13:56.607 --> 13:57.733
What?

159
13:59.902 --> 14:03.155
Hideo hasn't come home or sent word.

160
14:03.697 --> 14:06.033
I'm worried his pneumothorax might have returned.

161
14:06.116 --> 14:07.785
There's no need to worry.

162
14:08.410 --> 14:09.244
Understood.

163
14:11.205 --> 14:12.748
Have a good night.

164
14:32.267 --> 14:33.102
So-ran.

165
14:34.520 --> 14:35.354
Yes?

166
14:40.359 --> 14:41.944
Give me your hand for a second.

167
14:54.498 --> 14:57.710
I thought I'd get you something for tomorrow's banquet.

168
14:57.793 --> 14:59.420
I hope you like it.

169
15:00.921 --> 15:02.089
Thank you.

170
15:16.395 --> 15:18.272
Don't worry about tomorrow's mission.

171
15:18.772 --> 15:20.149
We'll pull it off for sure.

172
15:20.983 --> 15:23.360
We're going to the Government-General tomorrow.

173
15:23.444 --> 15:25.070
There's no telling what might happen.

174
15:32.202 --> 15:33.704
Do you remember what you said?

175
15:36.165 --> 15:39.001
You said you'd take your own life after killing Sato.

176
15:43.839 --> 15:45.340
I wanted to ask you something.

177
15:46.467 --> 15:49.970
"Is there really no place for me in your world?"

178
15:58.103 --> 15:59.521
You know how I feel about you, don't you?

179
16:01.690 --> 16:03.609
We may be posing as a married couple,

180
16:03.692 --> 16:06.195
but my feelings for you have always been real.

181
16:09.948 --> 16:10.783
I'm sorry.

182
16:17.915 --> 16:18.916
I understand.

183
16:29.301 --> 16:32.805
But this mission is different from the last one we carried out here.

184
16:33.514 --> 16:35.724
This one's a time bomb. You can make it out alive.

185
16:40.479 --> 16:43.190
It's okay if you don't feel the same way about me.

186
16:43.273 --> 16:45.818
Just don't even think about killing yourself after this mission.

187
16:47.444 --> 16:48.737
Philip.

188
16:49.363 --> 16:51.698
-So-ran. -I hope you understand.

189
16:54.660 --> 16:56.495
After everything I've been through,

190
16:58.622 --> 17:00.207
I think I'm a little exhausted.

191
17:06.088 --> 17:09.633
Do you remember my request to be cremated in hanbok?

192
17:11.260 --> 17:13.846
I should've prepared it beforehand, but I couldn't.

193
17:15.180 --> 17:16.765
Please, I'm counting on you.

194
17:26.733 --> 17:30.696
We'll pull this off, and you'll make it out alive.

195
17:30.779 --> 17:34.032
If we fail, and that's a big if,

196
17:34.658 --> 17:36.410
I won't let you get hurt. Ever.

197
18:07.524 --> 18:08.358
Come in.

198
18:12.696 --> 18:13.530
Hey.

199
18:14.239 --> 18:17.117
Put your things in here and take it with you.

200
18:20.370 --> 18:21.455
Thank you.

201
18:25.042 --> 18:28.045
Go to Gyeongseong Station right after the operation tomorrow.

202
18:29.087 --> 18:32.216
Go straight to Incheon and get on the morning boat.

203
18:33.550 --> 18:34.384
I will.

204
18:34.468 --> 18:36.428
Even if things don't go as planned,

205
18:37.387 --> 18:38.472
you'll still leave.

206
18:40.307 --> 18:41.642
Because that was our deal.

207
18:45.771 --> 18:47.981
Thank you for everything.

208
18:57.783 --> 19:01.036
What are you going to do after the mission?

209
19:02.704 --> 19:03.580
I'm not sure.

210
19:05.040 --> 19:06.917
I've never thought about it.

211
19:08.460 --> 19:10.379
You can figure it out when it's over.

212
19:11.922 --> 19:12.756
I suppose so.

213
19:15.050 --> 19:16.843
All right, then. Sleep well.

214
19:16.927 --> 19:19.513
You may not get much rest for a while, starting tomorrow.

215
19:21.598 --> 19:22.683
Madam.

216
19:24.393 --> 19:25.269
Yeah?

217
19:27.854 --> 19:28.689
Tomorrow…

218
19:30.649 --> 19:32.734
everything will go just fine.

219
19:34.236 --> 19:35.070
I hope so.

220
19:37.114 --> 19:37.948
Thanks.

221
20:09.438 --> 20:12.524
You could become a suspect after the operation tomorrow.

222
20:14.526 --> 20:16.570
Do you think I haven't prepared myself for that?

223
20:18.905 --> 20:21.241
You kept sneaking out alone,

224
20:22.826 --> 20:24.995
so I followed you to see if you had a lover.

225
20:27.122 --> 20:29.082
That eventually led me to the Gugukdan.

226
20:32.044 --> 20:32.878
You see,

227
20:34.212 --> 20:37.132
I didn't join the independence movement lightly.

228
20:39.551 --> 20:40.635
I know.

229
20:47.726 --> 20:49.436
Please don't get married, miss.

230
20:54.983 --> 20:56.610
Once tomorrow's operation is over,

231
20:58.362 --> 20:59.654
leave for Shanghai.

232
21:03.575 --> 21:04.826
With me.

233
21:17.297 --> 21:18.715
-Songjeon. -Hey.

234
21:21.051 --> 21:22.386
Let's eat.

235
21:22.469 --> 21:23.470
Here you go.

236
21:25.847 --> 21:26.681
Rice balls?

237
21:27.849 --> 21:29.518
-Did you make these? -Yeah.

238
21:30.185 --> 21:31.561
You said back in Yokohama,

239
21:31.645 --> 21:33.814
your mother's rice balls were your favorite.

240
21:35.524 --> 21:38.276
This is all the rice I could get.

241
21:40.904 --> 21:42.489
Come back safely tomorrow.

242
21:47.577 --> 21:48.412
Back then,

243
21:49.788 --> 21:50.997
when the earthquake hit…

244
21:53.542 --> 21:54.960
I lost my whole family…

245
21:57.462 --> 22:00.757
and I nearly got killed by the vigilante group.

246
22:02.551 --> 22:05.512
You told them I was Japanese, and that's what saved my life.

247
22:08.306 --> 22:09.724
I was truly

248
22:10.475 --> 22:11.726
grateful.

249
22:15.188 --> 22:16.440
I should be thanking you…

250
22:19.776 --> 22:20.652
for accepting me…

251
22:22.821 --> 22:24.322
as your friend.

252
22:29.244 --> 22:30.704
The rice will dry out.

253
22:30.787 --> 22:31.621
Eat up.

254
22:44.217 --> 22:45.093
That's so good.

255
22:46.761 --> 22:47.596
But…

256
22:49.473 --> 22:50.432
you got any kimchi?

257
22:51.933 --> 22:53.226
Rice balls go best with kimchi.

258
22:53.310 --> 22:54.436
Kimchi?

259
22:55.145 --> 22:56.938
No, we're all out.

260
23:00.108 --> 23:01.026
Hey, Songjeon.

261
23:02.360 --> 23:03.361
I mean, Mr. Matsuda.

262
23:03.445 --> 23:06.656
What do you mean, kimchi? Don't blow your cover.

263
23:12.996 --> 23:14.080
All right, let's eat.

264
23:55.038 --> 23:58.124
Wipe them clean. I don't want a single fingerprint!

265
24:00.794 --> 24:01.628
Hey!

266
24:02.170 --> 24:04.047
I told you not to leave fingerprints!

267
24:39.749 --> 24:40.750
Good morn…

268
24:46.756 --> 24:47.799
Good morning, sir.

269
24:51.177 --> 24:53.597
I hear the French technician praised your English

270
24:54.180 --> 24:56.391
to the chief of Foreign Affairs.

271
24:58.977 --> 25:01.396
You seem to get along well with foreigners.

272
25:02.981 --> 25:04.024
That's kind of you to say.

273
25:06.318 --> 25:07.402
Where'd you learn English?

274
25:08.486 --> 25:09.738
I picked it up as a child

275
25:10.697 --> 25:13.533
while working as a live-in maid for foreigners.

276
25:14.409 --> 25:17.454
I'd interpret for the lady of the house when she went to the market.

277
25:24.169 --> 25:25.754
So that's why

278
25:26.379 --> 25:29.341
you interpreted so well for that subversive before.

279
25:31.635 --> 25:32.469
Yes.

280
25:32.552 --> 25:33.762
His name was

281
25:34.471 --> 25:36.264
Keum Seok-jung, wasn't it?

282
25:38.391 --> 25:40.935
I don't remember his name clearly.

283
25:41.686 --> 25:42.687
Oh, is that so?

284
25:43.855 --> 25:45.523
Isn't Keum rather a rare surname?

285
25:45.607 --> 25:48.026
I'm surprised you don't remember.

286
25:48.818 --> 25:50.945
I was too nervous while interpreting,

287
25:51.738 --> 25:53.740
so his name didn't stick.

288
25:54.282 --> 25:56.868
He was nothing more than a subversive, after all.

289
25:56.951 --> 25:59.079
You said it was easy since you had so much experience.

290
26:00.246 --> 26:02.123
But you were too nervous to remember his name?

291
26:04.459 --> 26:05.293
It's just--

292
26:08.546 --> 26:09.923
Of course you were nervous.

293
26:10.674 --> 26:12.842
Jongno Police Station isn't just any local market.

294
26:14.969 --> 26:15.804
Indeed.

295
26:16.596 --> 26:18.723
You'll interpret for the foreign reporters

296
26:18.807 --> 26:20.225
at today's opening ceremony.

297
26:22.894 --> 26:23.728
Me?

298
26:25.313 --> 26:27.232
What about Interpreter Sato?

299
26:27.315 --> 26:29.901
He's called in sick. I hear a cold is going around.

300
26:31.986 --> 26:34.572
The pneumatic tube system opening ceremony is an important event.

301
26:34.656 --> 26:35.657
I'm assigning it to you

302
26:35.740 --> 26:38.660
since we couldn't find an interpreter for the technical terms right away.

303
26:39.452 --> 26:41.579
Be sure not to make a single mistake.

304
26:43.373 --> 26:44.374
Yes, sir.

305
26:44.457 --> 26:45.291
Very well.

306
26:51.673 --> 26:54.342
ENGLISH TRANSLATION UNIT

307
27:01.766 --> 27:04.185
INTERPRETER SATO HIDEO

308
27:11.568 --> 27:12.652
Hurry up!

309
27:43.558 --> 27:45.518
I don't get to see him before I leave.

310
27:59.449 --> 28:01.618
I wanted to help him find his mother.

311
29:32.458 --> 29:33.835
You'll be leaving today, right?

312
29:33.918 --> 29:34.752
Yes.

313
29:35.920 --> 29:37.046
I'm so jealous.

314
29:37.755 --> 29:40.174
You can just turn your back on Joseon and leave.

315
29:43.553 --> 29:45.722
I'm just as jealous of you.

316
29:47.223 --> 29:49.434
You have wealth, beauty,

317
29:49.517 --> 29:51.227
and someone good by your side.

318
29:51.978 --> 29:53.396
What? Someone good?

319
29:55.899 --> 29:58.401
I'm saying you're lucky to have everything.

320
29:59.235 --> 30:00.069
If you'll excuse me.

321
30:08.786 --> 30:11.497
Who would've thought Keijo would have a pneumatic tube system?

322
30:11.581 --> 30:14.667
It fills me with pride to see the Empire's greatness

323
30:14.751 --> 30:17.045
displayed to the world.

324
30:17.128 --> 30:20.673
The pneumatic tube system in Keijo isn't just an administrative infrastructure.

325
30:20.757 --> 30:23.217
The banquet is quite splendid.

326
30:25.720 --> 30:26.888
That's good to hear.

327
30:30.725 --> 30:31.851
Mr. Kim.

328
30:31.935 --> 30:34.145
You're quite the businessman.

329
30:34.228 --> 30:38.024
I knew it when you made the enormous donation to the pneumatic tube project.

330
30:38.107 --> 30:40.443
And now you've become the inspector general's in-law.

331
30:40.526 --> 30:42.070
There's no denying

332
30:42.153 --> 30:44.781
you're the star of tonight's banquet.

333
30:46.199 --> 30:47.408
Excuse me for a moment.

334
30:47.492 --> 30:48.326
Sure.

335
30:51.371 --> 30:52.288
Inspector general.

336
30:55.375 --> 30:58.044
Welcome, Mr. Yoo Philip.

337
30:58.628 --> 30:59.462
Mrs. Yoo.

338
31:00.046 --> 31:01.798
How have you been, Inspector General?

339
31:01.881 --> 31:03.883
It's an honor to be invited. Thank you.

340
31:03.967 --> 31:07.303
This event wouldn't mean as much without you, Mr. Yoo.

341
31:09.263 --> 31:12.350
I'll write an excellent article about the pneumatic tube opening ceremony.

342
31:12.433 --> 31:13.601
The whole world will see it

343
31:13.685 --> 31:16.521
and be amazed to see how developed Joseon has become.

344
31:18.272 --> 31:19.482
I'll look forward to it.

345
31:22.694 --> 31:25.905
I'm deeply sorry about what happened to your baby.

346
31:29.617 --> 31:33.913
There's no greater pain for a parent than losing a child.

347
31:43.464 --> 31:45.049
By the way, Inspector General,

348
31:45.133 --> 31:47.260
-about the opening ceremony-- -Yes.

349
31:48.678 --> 31:49.887
Thank you

350
31:50.805 --> 31:51.806
for your kind words.

351
31:53.725 --> 31:55.601
I'm back, sir.

352
31:56.644 --> 31:57.562
There you are.

353
31:59.063 --> 31:59.897
Hello, sir.

354
32:00.815 --> 32:01.691
We just arrived.

355
32:03.151 --> 32:04.944
During the opening ceremony,

356
32:05.028 --> 32:07.822
Ms. Keum will interpret for the foreign press.

357
32:10.199 --> 32:11.826
What a great honor.

358
32:11.909 --> 32:14.162
But Seo-hee's skills are rather limited yet,

359
32:14.245 --> 32:15.705
so that worries me.

360
32:15.788 --> 32:18.374
I believe Mr. Hideo should do it instead.

361
32:18.458 --> 32:19.292
Actually,

362
32:20.001 --> 32:23.171
Hideo called in sick with a cold today.

363
32:24.672 --> 32:26.299
Well, I suppose we have no choice, then.

364
32:28.760 --> 32:29.719
Inspector General.

365
32:31.054 --> 32:32.597
If you'll excuse me.

366
32:32.680 --> 32:35.141
Yoon Deog-yeong of the Central Advisory Council is here.

367
32:35.224 --> 32:36.392
Sure.

368
32:41.939 --> 32:43.066
You have to interpret today?

369
32:47.070 --> 32:47.945
Keum Seo-hee.

370
32:56.454 --> 32:57.997
Oh dear, what do I do?

371
32:58.081 --> 32:58.915
Where did it go?

372
32:58.998 --> 33:00.208
There it is.

373
33:02.376 --> 33:03.628
What's going on?

374
33:05.421 --> 33:08.424
Mrs. Yoo's button came off.

375
33:09.467 --> 33:11.094
There's a sewing kit in the office.

376
33:11.177 --> 33:13.054
May I take her to the office and help her?

377
33:13.137 --> 33:14.639
Then who's going to interpret?

378
33:15.640 --> 33:16.557
I'll do it.

379
33:22.647 --> 33:23.481
Go on, then.

380
33:24.482 --> 33:25.608
Thank you.

381
33:27.485 --> 33:28.486
Well then.

382
33:32.448 --> 33:34.075
Sorry about the commotion.

383
33:34.158 --> 33:35.535
It's quite all right.

384
33:37.495 --> 33:40.998
By the way, where is Hideo?

385
33:42.125 --> 33:43.084
Hideo is--

386
33:43.167 --> 33:45.086
Good evening, everyone!

387
33:45.795 --> 33:47.630
Hello, how are you all?

388
33:48.214 --> 33:49.507
It's been a long time.

389
33:50.716 --> 33:52.468
Hello, it's good to see you again.

390
33:59.559 --> 34:00.935
Is that Hideo?

391
34:02.478 --> 34:03.729
Hello.

392
34:03.813 --> 34:04.939
Good evening.

393
34:05.022 --> 34:06.232
Thanks.

394
34:07.024 --> 34:09.610
Good evening.

395
34:14.699 --> 34:18.828
Father, whom I respect above all others.

396
34:18.911 --> 34:21.414
There you are.

397
34:22.707 --> 34:26.502
I'm a little lat…

398
34:26.586 --> 34:28.254
No, wrong word. I meant "a little bit."

399
34:28.337 --> 34:29.255
I'm a little bit late.

400
34:32.383 --> 34:34.969
I always thought Hideo was a goody-goody.

401
34:35.052 --> 34:37.305
It turns out he's quite the man.

402
34:38.181 --> 34:39.015
Yes, I am.

403
34:40.308 --> 34:42.018
Myung-nam, where have you been?

404
34:42.685 --> 34:43.978
Why are you standing there?

405
34:44.061 --> 34:46.606
Why don't you come over and say hi to Hideo?

406
34:49.483 --> 34:50.610
Good evening.

407
34:50.693 --> 34:51.986
There, there.

408
34:52.069 --> 34:55.031
You two make such a lovely couple.

409
34:55.114 --> 34:56.365
I couldn't agree more.

410
34:57.658 --> 34:59.577
How could we not make a lovely couple?

411
34:59.660 --> 35:01.621
My father, whom I deeply respect,

412
35:01.704 --> 35:04.749
and Mr. Kim arranged this marriage.

413
35:04.832 --> 35:06.500
Exactly.

414
35:06.584 --> 35:08.252
You two look wonderful together.

415
35:08.336 --> 35:10.588
Oh, to be young.

416
35:12.882 --> 35:15.218
Yeah, all I have to do

417
35:15.301 --> 35:17.303
is do as I'm told.

418
35:18.512 --> 35:21.599
What should we name our baby?

419
35:22.183 --> 35:23.059
If it's a girl,

420
35:23.643 --> 35:24.477
Haruko?

421
35:25.228 --> 35:26.479
Akiko?

422
35:26.562 --> 35:27.688
"Ko" for "nose"?

423
35:28.272 --> 35:31.943
Well, Hideo, I think you've had a bit much to drink.

424
35:32.693 --> 35:33.527
Father.

425
35:33.611 --> 35:36.447
I'm doing well, aren't I?

426
35:36.530 --> 35:38.491
I'm doing everything you told me to do!

427
35:39.825 --> 35:41.077
Isn't that right?

428
35:49.669 --> 35:52.380
You're still going strong.

429
35:53.047 --> 35:55.174
What kind of behavior is this, Sato Hideo?

430
35:56.801 --> 35:58.427
"Sato Hideo."

431
35:58.511 --> 35:59.470
What?

432
36:00.388 --> 36:02.181
You don't have to remind me.

433
36:04.684 --> 36:07.061
I know my own name perfectly well.

434
36:19.657 --> 36:20.825
Take it to the banquet.

435
36:21.617 --> 36:23.286
You never know what might happen.

436
36:23.869 --> 36:27.957
We'll discuss the consequences of your behavior after the banquet.

437
37:05.870 --> 37:10.041
I heard there was quite a spectacle at the banquet, so I was on my way there.

438
37:12.293 --> 37:14.420
And here I've run into the star of the show.

439
37:16.714 --> 37:20.051
I made sure there'd be no disturbance outside.

440
37:21.552 --> 37:24.138
Little did I know the real trouble would be in here.

441
37:26.807 --> 37:28.642
So much for

442
37:29.268 --> 37:31.062
all that effort.

443
37:32.063 --> 37:33.189
Hideo.

444
37:33.272 --> 37:35.358
You should show proper respect

445
37:35.983 --> 37:37.818
when addressing your superior's son.

446
37:38.402 --> 37:41.447
Don't call me Hideo. It's Mr. Sato, you little shit.

447
37:45.034 --> 37:48.162
You and I are both Japan's dogs.

448
37:48.871 --> 37:50.998
Let's not bite each other.

449
38:13.521 --> 38:15.689
You're wearing earrings today.

450
38:20.027 --> 38:22.279
They don't seem like your style.

451
38:23.572 --> 38:24.824
Someone bought them for you?

452
38:27.201 --> 38:29.578
Was it Mr. Yoo?

453
38:35.167 --> 38:36.419
I got one done.

454
38:38.295 --> 38:39.213
Okay.

455
38:43.884 --> 38:45.261
They look good on you.

456
38:46.262 --> 38:47.096
They're pretty.

457
38:48.305 --> 38:50.975
So, why didn't Sato Hideo come to work today?

458
38:53.352 --> 38:54.645
I have no idea.

459
38:54.728 --> 38:56.856
But it's probably for the best.

460
38:56.939 --> 38:58.816
You can assemble them here.

461
38:58.899 --> 39:01.861
This is better than the restroom.

462
39:09.618 --> 39:10.828
Who is it?

463
39:16.417 --> 39:17.918
Who is it?

464
39:18.002 --> 39:18.919
It's me.

465
39:20.546 --> 39:21.464
Open the door.

466
39:22.006 --> 39:23.174
Why's the door locked?

467
39:23.757 --> 39:25.050
Yes, Interpreter Sato.

468
39:27.970 --> 39:30.514
Mrs. Yoo's button fell off.

469
39:30.598 --> 39:32.808
I'm sewing it back on for her. Just a moment.

470
39:32.892 --> 39:33.726
Wait. Just one more.

471
39:33.809 --> 39:35.478
-It'll be quick. -No, he's right outside.

472
39:36.479 --> 39:37.688
Who could be in there?

473
39:39.064 --> 39:39.982
Dad.

474
39:40.065 --> 39:41.692
We can look around another time.

475
39:41.775 --> 39:43.277
Nonsense, why wait?

476
39:43.360 --> 39:46.238
I just want to have a look at my son-in-law's office.

477
39:46.322 --> 39:48.199
Surely you can't make me turn back at the door.

478
39:48.282 --> 39:49.825
Don't you agree?

479
39:51.118 --> 39:52.161
That's right.

480
40:01.212 --> 40:03.130
Who's inside? Why the wait?

481
40:03.756 --> 40:05.090
Please bear with us for a moment.

482
40:06.258 --> 40:07.259
Come on, Dad.

483
40:19.104 --> 40:19.939
Mr. Sato.

484
40:20.856 --> 40:22.441
You're here.

485
40:22.525 --> 40:23.901
Let's go in.

486
40:25.903 --> 40:28.614
And at last, here we are!

487
40:29.865 --> 40:32.743
This is my son-in-law's office.

488
40:37.540 --> 40:40.960
You know how well my son-in-law speaks English?

489
40:41.502 --> 40:44.505
If Hideo succeeds me,

490
40:44.588 --> 40:48.759
Joil Textile Factory will be more successful than ever!

491
40:50.511 --> 40:52.596
You must feel very reassured.

492
40:53.264 --> 40:54.557
I'm really envious.

493
40:54.640 --> 40:55.766
I'll do my best.

494
40:55.849 --> 40:57.017
I'd appreciate your guidance.

495
40:59.186 --> 41:00.854
By the way, who is this lady?

496
41:01.772 --> 41:02.773
This is--

497
41:02.856 --> 41:06.318
She's the wife of Yoo Philip, an American correspondent from WWP News.

498
41:07.319 --> 41:09.572
An American reporter's wife?

499
41:10.531 --> 41:11.865
What was she doing here?

500
41:11.949 --> 41:14.577
I was helping her repair a button on her clothes.

501
41:15.160 --> 41:16.620
It's done now, you may leave.

502
41:22.668 --> 41:23.502
Wait.

503
41:24.378 --> 41:26.213
Why isn't that maid going with her?

504
41:26.297 --> 41:28.674
-This is-- -Sorry for the late introduction.

505
41:28.757 --> 41:31.844
I'm working alongside Mr. Sato as an interpreter trainee.

506
41:32.761 --> 41:34.430
A female interpreter?

507
41:34.930 --> 41:38.642
Well, if Hideo is training you, I suppose there's little to worry.

508
41:39.226 --> 41:42.271
Even so, isn't it a bit inappropriate for a man and a woman

509
41:42.354 --> 41:43.814
to share an office every day?

510
41:46.650 --> 41:47.651
In any case,

511
41:47.735 --> 41:50.821
look at Myung-nam and Hideo.

512
41:50.904 --> 41:53.490
They're a picture-perfect pair, aren't they?

513
41:53.574 --> 41:54.408
Absolutely.

514
41:56.744 --> 42:00.080
Myung-nam, stand a little closer to Hideo.

515
42:02.583 --> 42:06.295
She's never been around any men except for me,

516
42:06.378 --> 42:08.422
so she's terribly shy.

517
42:10.674 --> 42:11.508
Right.

518
42:11.592 --> 42:13.761
Why don't you link arms like you did before?

519
42:13.844 --> 42:15.512
Like a happy couple.

520
42:18.265 --> 42:19.183
Here, take my arm.

521
42:23.520 --> 42:25.731
There we go!

522
42:25.814 --> 42:28.192
A man ought to know how to take charge.

523
42:29.735 --> 42:32.446
He's charismatic and lacks for nothing.

524
42:32.529 --> 42:34.823
Absolutely. I'll make sure Myung-nam learns

525
42:34.907 --> 42:37.743
how to make a good hangover soup before they get married.

526
42:37.826 --> 42:38.661
Already?

527
42:40.079 --> 42:41.038
Myung-nam.

528
42:41.121 --> 42:44.291
You should come with us to the pneumatic tube opening ceremony.

529
42:45.793 --> 42:46.669
Me?

530
42:50.756 --> 42:54.009
You told me to wait in the banquet hall because that place is cramped.

531
42:54.093 --> 42:56.845
You should see this marvelous new technology

532
42:56.929 --> 42:58.347
that I'm funding, right?

533
42:58.931 --> 43:01.517
So I asked your father-in-law for a special favor.

534
43:02.935 --> 43:05.229
It must be nice to call him your in-law.

535
43:06.146 --> 43:07.272
He's right.

536
43:07.356 --> 43:10.192
Your father spent a whopping 100,000 won on the project.

537
43:10.275 --> 43:11.860
You should see it for yourself.

538
43:11.944 --> 43:14.196
I get uncomfortable in tight spaces.

539
43:14.279 --> 43:15.489
I'll stay in the banquet hall.

540
43:15.572 --> 43:16.615
Why's that?

541
43:16.699 --> 43:18.617
Do you have something to do there?

542
43:23.497 --> 43:24.373
Not really.

543
43:25.332 --> 43:26.500
Okay. I'll go with you.

544
43:26.583 --> 43:27.584
Very well.

545
43:27.668 --> 43:30.129
Your father-in-law is being so thoughtful.

546
43:30.212 --> 43:31.588
You should certainly come.

547
43:33.382 --> 43:34.466
You can go on ahead.

548
43:34.550 --> 43:36.051
I'll get changed and join you.

549
43:36.135 --> 43:38.053
Sure. Take your time.

550
43:38.137 --> 43:39.346
Now, let's head down.

551
43:39.430 --> 43:40.264
Let's go.

552
43:55.279 --> 43:57.614
I heard you weren't coming today.

553
43:59.616 --> 44:00.492
But here you are.

554
44:02.953 --> 44:04.121
Mr. Sato.

555
44:05.164 --> 44:06.123
Your lips…

556
44:11.378 --> 44:13.839
Have you been drinking?

557
44:15.174 --> 44:16.800
That's none of your business.

558
44:20.637 --> 44:21.472
What?

559
44:23.474 --> 44:25.434
Do you want to call me a pathetic loser

560
44:26.226 --> 44:28.687
who gets drunk and goes around picking fights

561
44:29.646 --> 44:30.981
because my father chewed me out?

562
44:32.566 --> 44:33.400
Mr. Sato.

563
44:33.484 --> 44:35.778
Do you think you've got me all figured out?

564
44:35.861 --> 44:38.739
So you think you can stick your nose into my business?

565
44:50.125 --> 44:51.084
I'm sorry.

566
44:52.252 --> 44:54.713
I had no right to pry.

567
44:57.508 --> 44:59.426
I'll head downstairs.

568
45:00.010 --> 45:01.094
I'll leave you alone.

569
45:10.813 --> 45:11.647
Hold on.

570
45:13.690 --> 45:14.817
What's this here?

571
45:26.495 --> 45:27.329
Sorry?

572
45:27.412 --> 45:28.622
This.

573
45:29.498 --> 45:30.624
This pawn ticket.

574
45:32.251 --> 45:33.669
Why'd you put it here?

575
45:36.129 --> 45:37.589
Why give it back out of the blue?

576
45:38.090 --> 45:39.925
Are you going somewhere? Or…

577
45:44.471 --> 45:46.014
do you not want anything to do

578
45:47.641 --> 45:49.476
with someone like me anymore?

579
45:55.566 --> 45:58.235
I think it's time I gave this back to you.

580
46:01.196 --> 46:04.366
You have your own path, and I have mine.

581
46:04.449 --> 46:06.034
We each have our own way to go.

582
46:09.580 --> 46:14.418
I know I've overstepped my bounds. Thank you for putting up with me.

583
46:15.752 --> 46:17.004
Thank you for everything.

584
46:32.060 --> 46:33.562
I liked you.

585
46:38.358 --> 46:41.653
Though I'd never see you again after tomorrow.

586
46:42.905 --> 46:43.906
I liked

587
46:45.574 --> 46:48.535
for who you were as Kim Tae-ung.

588
46:58.045 --> 47:00.631
I guess that's why I couldn't help getting involved.

589
47:12.309 --> 47:13.143
My name is…

590
47:14.770 --> 47:16.063
Sato Hideo.

591
47:20.859 --> 47:22.110
I'm not Kim Tae-ung.

592
48:01.942 --> 48:03.694
The opening ceremony will wrap up…

593
48:05.821 --> 48:08.281
with the governor-general receiving a congratulatory message

594
48:08.365 --> 48:11.702
from the Japanese Prime Minister via pneumatic tube from the Keijo Post Office.

595
48:13.870 --> 48:16.832
The very first item to arrive through the pneumatic tube

596
48:16.915 --> 48:19.751
that launched in Keijo today…

597
48:23.964 --> 48:28.260
The celebratory letter from Prime Minister Inukai!

598
48:33.557 --> 48:37.811
This just came from the Keijo Post Office!

599
48:43.442 --> 48:46.862
Then Ga-kyung will signal Songjeon.

600
48:46.945 --> 48:48.655
Please put me through to the kitchen.

601
48:49.364 --> 48:50.574
Yes, certainly.

602
48:50.657 --> 48:52.743
They must be parched.

603
48:53.785 --> 48:55.746
Understood. Thank you.

604
48:57.539 --> 49:00.876
His Excellency the Governor-General will head to the banquet hall in five minutes!

605
49:00.959 --> 49:02.085
-Yes, chef! -Yes, chef!

606
49:07.883 --> 49:09.134
Fire!

607
49:10.844 --> 49:11.970
Someone get water!

608
49:26.693 --> 49:27.903
What's going on?

609
49:33.909 --> 49:34.743
Yes, sir.

610
49:45.879 --> 49:47.047
Go see what's going on.

611
49:47.130 --> 49:47.964
Yes, sir.

612
49:49.841 --> 49:50.717
Is everything okay?

613
49:52.302 --> 49:54.930
Please remain calm, everyone!

614
49:56.473 --> 49:57.724
We're looking into it.

615
49:57.808 --> 49:58.892
Please wait a moment!

616
49:58.975 --> 50:00.727
Tell us what's going on!

617
50:13.406 --> 50:14.741
The bomb will explode

618
50:14.825 --> 50:17.744
during the governor-general's toast at the banquet.

619
50:17.828 --> 50:20.622
There are very important people upstairs.

620
50:21.206 --> 50:23.583
What were you thinking, setting off the alarm, you idiot?

621
50:23.667 --> 50:24.584
I'm sorry.

622
50:26.461 --> 50:27.337
What's going on?

623
50:28.672 --> 50:29.840
Nothing to worry about.

624
50:29.923 --> 50:32.050
Someone set off the fire alarm by mistake.

625
50:32.634 --> 50:34.511
Seriously, be more careful!

626
50:34.594 --> 50:35.428
Yes, sir.

627
50:38.181 --> 50:39.307
Everything's fine.

628
50:40.433 --> 50:41.643
Don't be concerned.

629
50:41.726 --> 50:42.978
There's no problem.

630
50:45.272 --> 50:46.273
Let's carry on.

631
50:54.739 --> 50:55.907
It was a false alarm.

632
50:56.491 --> 50:58.577
Everyone, there's no need to worry.

633
50:59.327 --> 51:01.454
The fire alarm was triggered by mistake.

634
51:04.875 --> 51:07.210
Please enjoy the rest of the evening.

635
51:09.880 --> 51:11.756
I heard you're from Shanghai.

636
51:14.843 --> 51:18.138
I used to live in Shanghai.

637
51:19.890 --> 51:21.099
I'm sorry.

638
51:21.183 --> 51:24.311
I don't speak Japanese well.

639
51:25.979 --> 51:29.149
I speak a little Chinese.

640
51:30.984 --> 51:35.530
Where in Shanghai did you live?

641
51:38.366 --> 51:39.826
-I-- -Oh my.

642
51:41.161 --> 51:42.287
One moment.

643
51:48.293 --> 51:49.794
What's the matter, ma'am?

644
52:03.934 --> 52:04.851
Maruyama.

645
52:05.435 --> 52:06.269
Yes, ma'am.

646
52:06.353 --> 52:08.230
Get these flowers out of here now.

647
52:11.274 --> 52:14.569
The governor-general gets hay fever from roses!

648
52:15.362 --> 52:17.781
What kind of secretary doesn't know that?

649
52:17.864 --> 52:19.908
He'll be here shortly.

650
52:19.991 --> 52:21.243
Get them out of here now!

651
52:21.326 --> 52:23.286
Right away! I'm so sorry!

652
52:31.086 --> 52:32.712
Sorry about that.

653
52:34.297 --> 52:38.635
Where in Shanghai did you live?

654
52:43.014 --> 52:45.141
Well then, let's head to the banquet hall.

655
53:13.211 --> 53:14.045
What?

656
53:31.521 --> 53:33.606
Darn it, why are these out here?

657
53:47.787 --> 53:48.997
What do I do with it?

658
53:59.591 --> 54:00.425
Watch out.

659
54:05.263 --> 54:06.389
You must be busy.

660
54:06.473 --> 54:07.891
Can I give you a hand?

661
54:07.974 --> 54:09.434
No, thanks.

662
54:12.562 --> 54:14.147
This cake is really…

663
54:15.857 --> 54:17.400
enormous.

664
54:17.484 --> 54:19.819
I've never seen a cake this big in my life.

665
54:19.903 --> 54:22.155
We got held up because of the fire alarm.

666
54:22.238 --> 54:24.199
Has the governor-general arrived yet?

667
54:24.282 --> 54:25.575
Not yet.

668
54:25.658 --> 54:26.701
That's a relief.

669
54:40.131 --> 54:42.050
The gift is in the cake.

670
55:11.663 --> 55:14.082
It'll go off at 6:20 p.m. Get as far away as you can.

671
55:20.171 --> 55:21.214
It's in the cake.

672
55:50.702 --> 55:53.955
His Excellency is here!

673
56:26.488 --> 56:30.992
Today, May 15th, 1932,

674
56:31.576 --> 56:33.578
Joseon's first pneumatic tube system

675
56:33.661 --> 56:36.372
has successfully been unveiled!

676
56:42.837 --> 56:47.217
The Great Japanese Empire's efforts for the development of Joseon

677
56:47.300 --> 56:51.554
have finally borne fruit today.

678
56:52.597 --> 56:53.556
This marks

679
56:54.265 --> 56:58.561
a new milestone in Joseon's modernization

680
56:59.103 --> 57:02.899
and the first step toward Manseon's prosperity…

681
57:04.234 --> 57:05.318
MANSEON MANCHURIA AND JOSEON

682
57:05.401 --> 57:07.737
…eventually reaching Manchukuo!

683
57:31.886 --> 57:33.555
Interpreter Sato!

684
57:35.098 --> 57:36.766
Interpreter Sato, over here.

685
57:46.276 --> 57:48.987
Interpret my speech into English.

686
57:50.113 --> 57:51.114
Yes, sir.

687
58:42.248 --> 58:43.124
Interpreter Sato.

688
58:45.877 --> 58:48.254
Why don't you join us for a toast?

689
58:53.092 --> 58:53.926
Yes, sir.

690
59:09.108 --> 59:10.360
Raise your glasses.

691
59:19.994 --> 59:22.497
It'll go off at 6:20 p.m. Get as far away as you can.

692
59:26.000 --> 59:27.251
Cheers!

693
59:28.169 --> 59:29.379
-Cheers! -Cheers!

694
01:00:19.137 --> 01:00:23.057
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

695
01:00:26.853 --> 01:00:29.230
There's no shortage of people who want me dead.

696
01:00:29.313 --> 01:00:31.190
Mr. Sato!

697
01:00:33.276 --> 01:00:35.278
We'll all get caught if we don't hurry.

698
01:00:35.361 --> 01:00:36.654
You should go already.

699
01:00:36.738 --> 01:00:37.989
I'm done going easy on you.

700
01:00:38.072 --> 01:00:38.906
Kill him.

701
01:00:40.658 --> 01:00:41.701
Don't forget.

702
01:00:41.784 --> 01:00:44.036
You're nobody if I'm dead.

703
01:00:44.120 --> 01:00:46.414
I'll make sure we catch the culprit tonight.

704
01:00:47.415 --> 01:00:48.499
Ga-kyung.

705
01:00:49.459 --> 01:00:50.752
Be happy.

706
01:00:58.134 --> 01:01:00.136
Subtitle translation by: Youji Kim
